module

public import Sheaf.RingTheory.SupportedHomogeneousDivision
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.MvPowerSeries.Substitution
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.MvPowerSeries.Order
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.MvPowerSeries.Trunc
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Flat.Basic
import Mathlib.RingTheory.FiniteType
import Mathlib.RingTheory.AdicCompletion.AsTensorProduct
import Mathlib.RingTheory.MvPowerSeries.Equiv

/-! # Coordinate-adic division and saturated blowup generators

Source: Bierstone--Milman, Invent. Math. 128 (1997), Lemma 7.22, (7.23),
Corollary 7.24, pp.269--270; ILO VIII 2.3.11--2.3.13, pp.93--94.
(blueprint: lem-trf-coordinate-blowup-division-generators)

The weight is one on the coordinate center and zero elsewhere. Its weighted order
is precisely the order for powers of the coordinate ideal, including infinity at zero.
Chart quotients are characterized by multiplication by the exceptional power; this
uniquely determines actual series and includes unit transforms and empty families.
The definitions below only package clauses of this theorem. They introduce no alternate
formal series, homogeneous division, substitution, or strict-transform construction.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false
noncomputable section
universe u v

namespace MonomialDiagram

/-- The supported expansions required of the ideal in the coordinate-division theorem.
This is a clause of its hypotheses, using the existing first-vertex quotient supports.
Source: BM (7.2)(3), Lemma 7.22
(blueprint: lem-trf-coordinate-blowup-division-generators). -/
def CoordinateSupportedGeneration {L : Type u} [Field L] {n s : ℕ}
    (α : Fin s → Fin n →₀ ℕ) (I : Ideal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) L))
    (F : Fin s → MvPowerSeries (Fin n) L) : Prop :=
  ∀ f ∈ I, ∃ q : Fin s → MvPowerSeries (Fin n) L,
    f = ∑ i : Fin s, q i * F i ∧
      ∀ (i : Fin s) (β : Fin n →₀ ℕ),
        MvPowerSeries.coeff β (q i) ≠ 0 → β ∈ quotientSupport α i

/-- The quotient estimate and the exact saturated-generator conclusion, in every chart.
The saturation is expressed by its defining membership condition, without choosing
an ideal representation. The last span is generated by all individual transforms.
Source: BM Lemma 7.22, (7.23), Corollary 7.24, pp.269--270; the scheme-theoretic
saturation convention of the DAG item
(blueprint: lem-trf-coordinate-blowup-division-generators). -/
def CoordinateBlowupDivisionProperties {L : Type u} [Field L] {n s : ℕ}
    (α : Fin s → Fin n →₀ ℕ) (I : Ideal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) L))
    (F : Fin s → MvPowerSeries (Fin n) L) (J : Finset (Fin n)) : Prop :=
  (∀ f ∈ I, ∃! q : Fin s → MvPowerSeries (Fin n) L,
    f = ∑ i : Fin s, q i * F i ∧
      ∀ (i : Fin s) (β : Fin n →₀ ℕ),
        MvPowerSeries.coeff β (q i) ≠ 0 → β ∈ quotientSupport α i) ∧
  (∀ (f : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) L), f ∈ I → f ≠ 0 →
    ∀ q : Fin s → MvPowerSeries (Fin n) L,
      f = ∑ i : Fin s, q i * F i →
      (∀ (i : Fin s) (β : Fin n →₀ ℕ),
        MvPowerSeries.coeff β (q i) ≠ 0 → β ∈ quotientSupport α i) →
      ∀ i : Fin s,
        f.weightedOrder (fun j ↦ if j ∈ J then 1 else 0) ≤
          (q i).weightedOrder (fun j ↦ if j ∈ J then 1 else 0) + (α i).degree) ∧
  ∀ (h : Fin n), h ∈ J → ∀ ξ : Fin n → L,
    ∃ G : Fin s → MvPowerSeries (Fin n) L,
      (∀ i : Fin s, MvPowerSeries.X h ^ (α i).degree * G i =
        MvPowerSeries.subst
          (fun j ↦ if j = h then MvPowerSeries.X h else
            if j ∈ J then MvPowerSeries.X h * (MvPowerSeries.C (ξ j) + MvPowerSeries.X j)
            else MvPowerSeries.X j) (F i)) ∧
      (∀ (f : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) L), f ∈ I → f ≠ 0 →
        ∃ g : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) L,
          MvPowerSeries.X h ^ (f.weightedOrder (fun j ↦ if j ∈ J then 1 else 0)).toNat * g =
            MvPowerSeries.subst
              (fun j ↦ if j = h then MvPowerSeries.X h else
                if j ∈ J then
                  MvPowerSeries.X h * (MvPowerSeries.C (ξ j) + MvPowerSeries.X j)
                else MvPowerSeries.X j) f) ∧
      (∀ g : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) L,
        (∃ m : ℕ, MvPowerSeries.X h ^ m * g ∈
          Ideal.span
            (MvPowerSeries.subst
              (fun j ↦ if j = h then MvPowerSeries.X h else
                if j ∈ J then
                  MvPowerSeries.X h * (MvPowerSeries.C (ξ j) + MvPowerSeries.X j)
                else MvPowerSeries.X j) '' (I : Set (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) L)))) ↔
          g ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range G)) ∧
      Ideal.span (Set.range G) = Ideal.span
        {g : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) L | ∃ f ∈ I, f ≠ 0 ∧
          MvPowerSeries.X h ^ (f.weightedOrder (fun j ↦ if j ∈ J then 1 else 0)).toNat * g =
            MvPowerSeries.subst
              (fun j ↦ if j = h then MvPowerSeries.X h else
                if j ∈ J then
                  MvPowerSeries.X h * (MvPowerSeries.C (ξ j) + MvPowerSeries.X j)
                else MvPowerSeries.X j) f}

/-- Coordinate-adic division estimates and finite generators for the saturated chart ideal.
The vertices are a finite ordered list (`Fin s`); their diagram and quotient supports
are `generated α` and `quotientSupport α`. The degree truncation of the homogeneous
component is exactly the initial homogeneous polynomial, not a further approximation.

Source: BM Lemma 7.22, (7.23), Corollary 7.24, pp.269--270; ILO VIII 2.3.11--2.3.13.
(blueprint: lem-trf-coordinate-blowup-division-generators)

Proof (DAG steps 1--8):
1. Let a be the least coordinate order of a nonzero quotient plus its generator degree.
If the coordinate-initial sum canceled, take its least total-degree part. It is a
nontrivial supported relation among the initial homogeneous forms, contradicting unique
homogeneous division. Thus ord_P(f)=a and every quotient has order at least v-d_i.
2. In the ratio chart C=A[X_j/e], every element is a/e^m with a in P^m, and conversely.
For a monomial of P-degree p, substitution and division by e^d give e^(p-d) times the
translated direction monomials and the outside-coordinate monomials. Its order is at
least its old total degree minus d. Each output jet therefore uses finitely many input
coefficients. This constructs the regular divided series for arbitrary scalars.
3. If T=IC:e^infinity, clear denominators to write each nonzero element as f/e^M with
f in I intersect P^M. The estimate in step 1 shows each quotient coefficient divided
by e^(M-d_i) belongs to C (multiply instead when M<d_i). Hence T=(F_i/e^d_i).
4. The coordinate-ratio-chart completion is B with exactly the displayed substitution
(lem-trf-coordinate-ratio-chart-completion). A is Noetherian by
lem-weil-pbc-power-series-noetherian, C is Noetherian by
lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-algebra-noetherian, and B is flat over C by
lem-weil-pbc-noetherian-completion-flat. Flatness of A to B is not needed.
5. Multiplication by e is injective on C/T. Tensor with flat B using
lem-trf-flat-tensor-preserves-injection; B tensor (C/T) is B/TB by the canonical balanced
maps b tensor c to bc and b to b tensor 1. Thus TB is e-saturated. Both inclusions
between TB and IB:e^infinity follow, since e^d_i times each generator lies in IB.
6. For nonzero f, divide each supported quotient by the permitted exceptional power
from step 1. Multiplying the resulting equality by e^v and using injectivity of
multiplication by e gives generation of its individual transform. Conversely each G_i
is an individual transform, so the two generated ideals coincide.
7. Over a coefficient-field extension the supported homogeneous matrices and their
inverses extend coefficientwise. Continuous homogeneous formal division
(lem-trf-homogeneous-continuous-formal-division) gives compatible supported quotients.
Polynomial multiples have zero remainder; continuity and multiplier truncation give
zero remainder on the entire extended ideal. Orders are preserved by injectivity on
coefficients. Apply steps 1--6 over the new field. Substitution and exact exceptional
division commute with extension because every output coefficient uses a finite jet.
8. For the zero ideal and empty family, no nonzero element occurs, the spans are zero,
and coefficient shifting makes multiplication by e injective, so saturation is zero.
There is no chart when n=0 and J is required nonempty. -/
theorem coordinate_blowup_division_generators
    {L : Type u} [Field L] [CharZero L] {n s : ℕ}
    (α : Fin s → Fin n →₀ ℕ) (hα : IsOrderedVertexFamily (generated α) α)
    (I : Ideal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) L)) (F : Fin s → MvPowerSeries (Fin n) L)
    (hmem : ∀ i : Fin s, F i ∈ I)
    (horder : ∀ i : Fin s, (F i).order = ((α i).degree : ℕ∞))
    (hdivision : ∀ t : ℕ, HasUniqueDivision (generated α) α
      (fun i ↦ MvPowerSeries.truncTotal ((α i).degree + 1)
        (MvPowerSeries.homogeneousComponent (α i).degree (F i))) t)
    (hgen : CoordinateSupportedGeneration α I F)
    (J : Finset (Fin n)) (hJ : J.Nonempty)
    (hP : ∀ i : Fin s, (F i).weightedOrder (fun j ↦ if j ∈ J then 1 else 0) =
      ((α i).degree : ℕ∞)) :
    CoordinateBlowupDivisionProperties α I F J ∧
    ∀ (E : Type v) [Field E] (φ : L →+* E),
      (∀ i : Fin s, (MvPowerSeries.map φ (F i)).order = ((α i).degree : ℕ∞)) ∧
      (∀ i : Fin s, (MvPowerSeries.map φ (F i)).weightedOrder
        (fun j ↦ if j ∈ J then 1 else 0) = ((α i).degree : ℕ∞)) ∧
      (∀ t : ℕ, HasUniqueDivision (generated α) α
        (fun i ↦ MvPowerSeries.truncTotal ((α i).degree + 1)
          (MvPowerSeries.homogeneousComponent (α i).degree (MvPowerSeries.map φ (F i)))) t) ∧
      CoordinateSupportedGeneration α (I.map (MvPowerSeries.map φ))
        (fun i ↦ MvPowerSeries.map φ (F i)) ∧
      CoordinateBlowupDivisionProperties α (I.map (MvPowerSeries.map φ))
        (fun i ↦ MvPowerSeries.map φ (F i)) J ∧
      (∀ (f : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) L) (q : Fin s → MvPowerSeries (Fin n) L),
        f ∈ I → f = ∑ i : Fin s, q i * F i →
        (∀ (i : Fin s) (β : Fin n →₀ ℕ),
          MvPowerSeries.coeff β (q i) ≠ 0 → β ∈ quotientSupport α i) →
        MvPowerSeries.map φ f =
          ∑ i : Fin s, MvPowerSeries.map φ (q i) * MvPowerSeries.map φ (F i) ∧
        ∀ (i : Fin s) (β : Fin n →₀ ℕ),
          MvPowerSeries.coeff β (MvPowerSeries.map φ (q i)) ≠ 0 →
            β ∈ quotientSupport α i) ∧
      (∀ (h : Fin n), h ∈ J → ∀ (ξ : Fin n → L) (f : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) L),
        MvPowerSeries.map φ (MvPowerSeries.subst
          (fun j ↦ if j = h then MvPowerSeries.X h else
            if j ∈ J then MvPowerSeries.X h * (MvPowerSeries.C (ξ j) + MvPowerSeries.X j)
            else MvPowerSeries.X j) f) =
          MvPowerSeries.subst
            (fun j ↦ if j = h then MvPowerSeries.X h else
              if j ∈ J then
                MvPowerSeries.X h * (MvPowerSeries.C (φ (ξ j)) + MvPowerSeries.X j)
              else MvPowerSeries.X j) (MvPowerSeries.map φ f)) ∧
      (∀ (h : Fin n), h ∈ J → ∀ ξ : Fin n → L,
        (Ideal.span {g : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) L | ∃ m : ℕ,
          MvPowerSeries.X h ^ m * g ∈ Ideal.span
            (MvPowerSeries.subst
              (fun j ↦ if j = h then MvPowerSeries.X h else
                if j ∈ J then
                  MvPowerSeries.X h * (MvPowerSeries.C (ξ j) + MvPowerSeries.X j)
                else MvPowerSeries.X j) '' (I : Set (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) L)))}).map
          (MvPowerSeries.map φ) =
        Ideal.span {g : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) E | ∃ m : ℕ,
          MvPowerSeries.X h ^ m * g ∈ Ideal.span
            (MvPowerSeries.subst
              (fun j ↦ if j = h then MvPowerSeries.X h else
                if j ∈ J then
                  MvPowerSeries.X h * (MvPowerSeries.C (φ (ξ j)) + MvPowerSeries.X j)
                else MvPowerSeries.X j) ''
                  (I.map (MvPowerSeries.map φ) : Set (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) E)))}) ∧
      (∀ (h : Fin n) (d : ℕ) (f g : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) L),
        MvPowerSeries.X h ^ d * g = f →
          MvPowerSeries.X h ^ d * MvPowerSeries.map φ g = MvPowerSeries.map φ f) := by
  sorry

end MonomialDiagram
